  "sources": "# Sources — 01 Seurat, A Sunday on La Grande Jatte — 1884\n\n## Facts\n- Title, dates (1884–86, border added 1888–89), oil on canvas, 207.5 × 308.1 cm, Helen Birch Bartlett Memorial Collection; many painted and drawn sketches plus larger canvases led up to it; Seurat reworked it two years after starting, adding the monkey and other figures; Greek-frieze ambition. Art Institute of Chicago API record: https://api.artic.edu/api/v1/artworks/27992 (page: https://www.artic.edu/artworks/27992/a-sunday-on-la-grande-jatte-1884)\n- Painted in two campaigns, May 1884–March 1885 and October 1885–May 1886; shown at the eighth and last Impressionist exhibition, May 1886; dotted border added 1888–89; zinc yellow darkened to brown, already visible in Seurat's lifetime; acquired 1924; Sondheim/Lapine musical *Sunday in the Park with George* (1984); class mix (Everdell, *The First Moderns*). https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Sunday_Afternoon_on_the_Island_of_La_Grande_Jatte\n- Zinc yellow (zinc potassium chromate) darkened soon after completion: AIC conservation pages, e.g. https://archive.artic.edu/sciarttech/2e3.html\n- 1886 show at 1 rue Laffitte opened May 15 without Monet, Renoir, Sisley or Caillebotte: https://www.britannica.com/art/the-eight-Impressionist-exhibitions — Neo-Impressionist works hung apart, *La Grande Jatte* dominated the room: https://www.britannica.com/biography/Camille-Pissarro/The-Impressionist-years\n- Félix Fénéon coined \"Neo-Impressionism\" in 1886: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo-impressionism\n- Seurat born 2 Dec 1859, died 29 Mar 1891 (aged 31); 24 when he began in May 1884: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georges_Seurat\n- Singesse slang and pêcher/pécher pun (hedged as \"many historians think\"): our reel script channels/art-history/episodes/001-seurat-monkey/script.md; the Wikipedia article above notes the fishing/prostitution allusion reading.\n\n## Images\n| File | Source | Licence |\n|---|---|---|\n| img/full.jpg, cover.jpg, class.jpg, grass.jpg, phone.jpg, border.jpg (crops) and dots.jpg, monkey.jpg, fisher.jpg (episode assets) | https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Sunday_on_La_Grande_Jatte,_Georges_Seurat,_1884.jpg | Public domain |\n| img/met_study.jpg — Study for \"A Sunday on La Grande Jatte\", 1884, The Met | https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Study_for_%22A_Sunday_on_La_Grande_Jatte%22_MET_DP259921.jpg | CC0 (Met Open Access) |\n| img/nga_study.jpg — Study for La Grande Jatte, 1884–85, NGA Washington | https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Study_for_La_Grande_Jatte,_Georges_Seurat,_1884.jpg | Public domain |\n| img/seated.jpg — Seated Woman with a Parasol (study), 1884/85, conté crayon, AIC | https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georges_Seurat_-_Seated_Woman_with_a_Parasol_(study_for_La_Grande_Jatte)_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg | Public domain |\n| img/seurat1888.jpg — photograph of Georges Seurat, c. 1888 (from Lucie Cousturier, *Seurat*) | https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georges_Seurat_1888.jpg | Public domain |\n| img/_raw/ng6556.jpg, ng6560.jpg, albright.jpg (downloaded, not used) | Commons: NG6556, NG6560, Albright–Knox 1948-7 | Public domain |\n"
