  "caption": "Someone else is in this room. Look in the mirror.\n\nJan van Eyck painted a merchant and his wife in Bruges in 1434, then hid two visitors in a convex mirror no bigger than your palm. One wears red. Above it, he wrote on the wall like graffiti: \"Jan van Eyck was here.\"\n\nOne lit candle in daylight. Oranges worth a fortune. Kicked-off shoes. And no, she's not pregnant.\n\nSwipe to read the room, then watch the reel and step inside the painting yourself. Save this for your next National Gallery visit.",
