  "museum": "Contarelli Chapel, San Luigi dei Francesi, Rome",
  "videoFormat": "Step inside the painting: 9:16 seamless flythrough loop",
  "hook": "Who's he pointing at?",
  "caption": "Who's he pointing at? 👉\n\nChrist walks into a Roman tax office and points. For 400 years everyone agreed the bearded man was Matthew, pointing at himself: \"Me?\" Then, in the 1980s, a few scholars said no. He's pointing at the boy counting coins, the one who won't look up.\n\nSwipe for the hands that borrow from Michelangelo, a beam of light that matches the chapel's real window, and the apostle the X-rays say wasn't there at first. Plus the painter who became famous overnight, then killed a man.\n\nSave this for your next trip to Rome, and watch the reel to step inside the painting.",
