  "hook": "He erased part of this room.",
  "caption": "He erased part of this room.\n\nDegas's The Rehearsal (c. 1873–78) hangs at Harvard. Look close and you'll find a lone violinist shoved into the corner, the 'petits rats' of the Paris Opéra at the barre, and a ghost: Harvard says Degas later painted out a whole stairwell. In his Glasgow version, that spiral stair survives, dancers' legs coming down it, cut off by the frame.\n\nHe wasn't backstage when he painted this. His dancers came to his studio to pose. And the men who were backstage? That's slide 5.\n\nSwipe to the end, then watch the reel: we flew a camera straight into the room. Save this for your next museum visit.",
