  "sources": "# Sources — 07 Degas, The Rehearsal\n\n## The painting\n- Edgar Degas, *The Rehearsal*, c. 1873–1878, oil on canvas, 47.2 × 61.5 cm. Harvard Art Museums/Fogg Museum, Bequest from the Collection of Maurice Wertheim, Class of 1906, 1951.47. https://harvardartmuseums.org/collections/object/303496\n  - Harvard: \"one of Degas's earliest paintings of dancers\"; a grid is visible under the paint; \"Degas later reworked this painting, taking out a stairwell and repositioning some of the figures.\"\n  - Catalogue raisonné (MS 220, dated c. 1873): https://www.degas-catalogue.com/en/artworks/la-repetition-220\n- IIIF manifest used to check images: https://iiif.harvardartmuseums.org/manifests/object/303496\n\n## Facts by slide\n- S3 violinist: visible in the painting; single-violin rehearsal accompaniment also shown in Degas's *The Dancing Class*, c. 1870 (Met 29.100.184/436141).\n- S4 petits rats, entry age ~7–8, lower-class origins: Corrinne Chong, review of *Degas à l'Opéra*, Nineteenth-Century Art Worldwide, Autumn 2020. https://www.19thc-artworldwide.org/autumn20/chong-reviews-degas-a-l-opera\n- S5 abonnés = wealthy subscribers with backstage access, \"preying upon young dancers\"; Degas could afford a subscription only in 1885 (\"three-day subscription\"): Chong 2020 (above). Orsay/NGA exhibition *Degas à l'Opéra* (2019–20).\n- S6 studio posing: The Met, *The Dancing Class*, c. 1870 — \"Because the artist did not yet have privileges to go backstage at the Paris Opéra, his subjects came to his studio to pose.\" https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/436141 (hedged on slide as \"Early on\").\n- S7 quote: Edmond de Goncourt, *Journal*, 1874 (13 Feb. 1874), after visiting Degas's studio: \"a world of pink and white, of female flesh in lawn and gauze\" — quoted on Harvard's object page (above).\n- S8 1870 eyesight: Met essay \"Edgar Degas (1834–1917): Painting and Drawing\" (eye trouble surfaced during his National Guard service in the 1870 siege of Paris). https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/edgar-degas-1834-1917-painting-and-drawing\n- S8 1874: Degas exhibited at the first Impressionist exhibition (Paris, April 1874) — same Met essay.\n- S8 1881: *Little Dancer Aged Fourteen* shown in wax at the Sixth Impressionist Exhibition, with real tutu, slippers, wig of human hair; hostile critics (e.g. Paul Mantz, Le Temps, 1881). NGA 1999.80.28 https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.110292.html ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Dancer_of_Fourteen_Years\n- S9 Glasgow version: Degas, *The Rehearsal*, c. 1874, Burrell Collection, Glasgow Museums (35.246), with spiral staircase and dancers' legs descending. https://artuk.org/discover/artworks/the-rehearsal-83736\n\n## Images\n| File | Source | Licence |\n|---|---|---|\n| img/full.jpg, cover.jpg, violinist*.jpg, p_*.jpg, left_half.jpg, window.jpg | our asset assets/degas/degas_rehearsal_fogg_full.jpg (Harvard Art Museums 1951.47) | Painting public domain; Harvard image terms: personal/educational noncommercial use |\n| img/burrell_full.jpg, burrell_stair.jpg | https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edgar_Degas,_The_Rehearsal,_c._1874..jpg (Burrell Collection, Glasgow) | Public domain (Wikimedia Commons) |\n| img/little_dancer.jpg | https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edgar_Degas,_Little_Dancer_Aged_Fourteen,_1878-1881,_NGA_110292.jpg (National Gallery of Art) | CC0 (NGA open access) |\n| img/met_dancing_class.jpg | https://images.metmuseum.org/CRDImages/ep/original/DP-25445-001.jpg — Met 436141, The Dancing Class, c. 1870 | CC0 (Met Open Access) |\n| img/first_frame.jpg | our asset assets/degas/rehearsal_first_frame_ai_1080.png (first frame of our film) | Ours |\n| img/_raw/met_dance_class_1874.jpg | Met 438817 (not used on slides) | CC0 |\n| img/_raw/huam_*.jpg | Harvard IIIF (nrs.harvard.edu) incl. X-radiograph STR007768 (not used: unreadable) | Harvard noncommercial terms |\n"
